<parameter name="content"># Deployment Guide for Access Request Recruiter Details Feature

## Frontend Changes
The feature has been implemented in `Frontend/src/pages/AccessRequestsManagement.jsx`:
- Added clickable recruiter names in the access requests table
- Created RecruiterProfileModal component with 5 tabs (Personal, Professional, Skills, Experience, Education)
- Added API call to fetch recruiter profiles

## Backend Requirements
Ensure the following API endpoint exists:
```
GET /api/profile/recruiter/:id
```

This endpoint should return recruiter profile data including:
- Personal info (name, email, phone, location, country, bio)
- Professional details (specialization, industries, methods, experience)
- Skills array
- Work experience array
- Education array

## Firebase Deployment Steps

### 1. Build the frontend
```bash
cd /Users/brandcatapult/Downloads/newrecuiterv/Frontend
npm run build
```

### 2. Deploy to Firebase Hosting
```bash
cd /Users/brandcatapult/Downloads/newrecuiterv
firebase deploy --only hosting
```

### 3. Or deploy the entire project
```bash
firebase deploy
```

## For Automatic Deployment
If you have CI/CD set up, commit and push to trigger automatic deployment:
```bash
git add .
git commit -m "Add recruiter profile details feature to access requests"
git push origin main
```

## Verification
After deployment, verify:
1. Access Requests Management page loads correctly
2. Clicking on recruiter name opens the profile modal
3. All tabs (Personal, Professional, Skills, Experience, Education) display correctly
4. Profile completion percentage shows correctly
